nbtstat Overview
nbtstat is primarily used to display NetBIOS name tables, resolve NetBIOS names, and check NetBIOS connections. It's not used for monitoring open ports in real time like netstat or ss.

Common nbtstat Commands:
nbtstat -n → Displays local NetBIOS names registered on the system.

nbtstat -c → Shows the NetBIOS name cache.

nbtstat -a <hostname> → Displays NetBIOS names of a remote machine.

nbtstat -A <IP address> → Similar to -a, but queries using an IP address.
