TCPView is a Windows utility that provides a real-time view of all TCP and UDP connections on your system, including listening ports, established connections, and remote addresses.

Key Features of TCPView:
Shows active and listening network connections.

Displays process names associated with each connection.

Updates in real-time (unlike netstat, which gives a snapshot).

Allows users to terminate connections or close processes directly.

How to Use TCPView:
Download TCPView from Microsoft Sysinternals.

Run Tcpview.exe (No installation required).

You’ll see a list of all active network connections, including:

Local and remote addresses

Port numbers

Connection states (LISTENING, ESTABLISHED, etc.)

Associated process names
